picocalc-os: on ESP-IDF, os_self_thread() returns the current FreeRTOS task handle instead of pthread_self(),
which asserts ("Failed to find current thread ID!") in a task that pthread_create did not make. picocalc-os runs
the runtime in its kernel task (xTaskCreatePinnedToCore). Without the thread manager the value is only compared
(exec_env->handle) and logged.

--- a/core/shared/platform/esp-idf/espidf_thread.c
+++ b/core/shared/platform/esp-idf/espidf_thread.c
@@ -33,9 +33,11 @@
 korp_tid
 os_self_thread(void)
 {
-    /* only allowed if this is a thread, xTaskCreate is not enough look at
-     * product_mini for how to use this*/
-    return pthread_self();
+    /* picocalc-os: the current FreeRTOS task, which works in any task;
+       pthread_self() asserts in a task that pthread_create did not make
+       (picocalc-os runs its kernel in one). Without the thread manager the
+       runtime only compares this value and logs it. */
+    return (korp_tid)(uintptr_t)xTaskGetCurrentTaskHandle();
 }
 
 int
